From: syabyr <syabyr@github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: multi: custom manufacturer and product strings

The LubanCat 1N exposes its Type-C download port through the built-in
g_multi composite gadget.  With the stock strings the device shows up
on a connected PC as "Linux Foundation Multifunction Composite Gadget":
the manufacturer string is empty, so the host falls back to the
VID 0x1d6b (Linux Foundation) database name, and the product string is
the generic driver description.

Give the device product-specific strings: manufacturer "Imotion",
product "bsAgent".  VID/PID are left untouched so host-side RNDIS
driver binding and usbutils device detection keep working.

Signed-off-by: syabyr <syabyr@github.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/multi.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/multi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/legacy/multi.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 #endif
 
 
-#define DRIVER_DESC		"Multifunction Composite Gadget"
+#define DRIVER_DESC		"bsAgent"
 
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION(DRIVER_DESC);
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Michal Nazarewicz");
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@
 };
 
 static struct usb_string strings_dev[] = {
-	[USB_GADGET_MANUFACTURER_IDX].s = "",
+	[USB_GADGET_MANUFACTURER_IDX].s = "Imotion",
 	[USB_GADGET_PRODUCT_IDX].s = DRIVER_DESC,
 	[USB_GADGET_SERIAL_IDX].s = "",
 	[MULTI_STRING_RNDIS_CONFIG_IDX].s = "Multifunction with RNDIS",
